          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Collect four cards of the same suit to maximize your score (maximum 41).',
          gameplay: "1. Turn: On your turn, you draw one card (from the Stock or the Discard Pile) and then discard one card face-up.\n2. One-Card Limit: You must always have exactly 4 cards at the end of your turn.\n3. The Stop: Any player who has four cards of the SAME SUIT can declare 'Stop' (Selesai). The hand ends immediately.",
          keyRules: [
            "You cannot pick up the previous player's discard and immediately discard it back.",
            'If the Stock runs out, the discard pile is shuffled to form a new Stock.',
            "If a player 'Stops' and their 4-card suit sum is lower than an opponent's mixed-hand sum, the stopper still wins the round in some house rules, but usually, the highest score wins regardless.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Commit early. If you are dealt two high cards of the same suit (e.g., A and Q of Clubs), discard everything else and hunt for Clubs immediately.',
          intermediate: "The Discard Signal: Pay attention to what your opponent discards. If they drop a King of Diamonds, itâ€™s a strong sign they are NOT collecting Diamonds. You can safely build a Diamond hand knowing they likely won't take your discards.",
          advanced: "Defensive Discarding: If you know the player to your left is collecting Spades, you should hold onto high Spades even if they don't fit your hand, to prevent them from hitting 41.",
          tips: [
            "Don't wait for 41. If you have 38 or 39, it's often better to Stop before an opponent manages to fix a messy hand.",
            'High cards (10s and Aces) are the only way to reach safe scores; dump low cards (2s and 3s) unless they are part of your core suit.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
